course: dictionary
lesson: 13826
title: A narrow land bridge
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Maps show many shapes of land and sea. An isthmus is a narrow strip of land with sea on both sides, and it joins two bigger pieces of land. «The road ran along the isthmus, with the sea on the left and the sea on the right.» The sea on both sides is the clue, and the narrow land in the middle is the bridge.
explain: Think of the opposite idea, a strait. A strait is a narrow sea that joins two seas. «The ferry crossed the strait between the two islands.» If the narrow part in the middle is land, it is an isthmus. If it is water, it is a strait.
explain: The word has a science meaning too. In the body or in a plant, an isthmus is a narrow part that joins two bigger parts. «The thin stalk was an isthmus joining the leaf to the rest of the plant.» Look for the word joins and the narrow middle part.
fact: An isthmus is a narrow strip of land with sea on both sides.
fact: An isthmus joins two bigger pieces of land.
fact: The Isthmus of Panama joins North and South America.
fact: The Panama Canal was cut through the Isthmus of Panama so ships could sail from one ocean to the other.
fact: Auckland, in New Zealand, stands on an isthmus.
exercise: «The Isthmus of Panama joins North and South America.» What is an isthmus? | A very tall mountain | *A narrow strip of land with sea on both sides | A narrow sea that joins two seas | A large island in the middle of an ocean
exercise: «The ferry crossed the strait between the two islands.» What is the opposite of an isthmus? | A desert | A bridge over a river | A deep valley | *A strait, a narrow sea joining two seas
exercise: Maya says an isthmus is a big lake. Why is she wrong? | She is right, it is a big lake | An isthmus is always a very high hill | An isthmus is a big lake in the middle of a city | *An isthmus is land, not water, and it is narrow with sea on both sides
test: «The Panama Canal was cut through the isthmus so ships could travel between two oceans.» What does isthmus mean? | A deep hole in the ground | A kind of boat | *A narrow strip of land joining two bigger pieces of land | A wide, calm sea
test: In science, «The narrow part joining the two bigger parts of the leaf was an isthmus.» What does isthmus mean in this sentence? | A large, empty space | A type of leaf | *A narrow part that joins two bigger parts | A small seed
exam: «Ferries sail through the strait, but cars drive across the isthmus.» Which word is land joining two bigger pieces of land? | strait | ferry | ocean | *isthmus
